  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REVIVING AND STRENGTHENING JOINT FOREST MANAGEMENT FOR THE PROMOTION AND LIVELIHOODS IN THE SRIVILLIPUTHER-MEGAMALAI TIGER RESERVE SMTR, TAMIL NADU, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO RESTORE TIGER HABITAT IN THE NEWLY DECLARED SRIVILLIPUTHUR-MEGAMALAI TIGER RESERVE (SMTR) IN TAMIL NADU. PROJECT ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: FORM JOINT FOREST MANAGEMENT COMMITTEES IN VILLAGES ADJACENT TO SMTR AND INVOLVE WOMEN ON THESE COMMITTEES, DEVELOP THE CAPACITIES OF FRONTLINE FOREST STAFF ON FOREST MANAGEMENT, PROVIDE ALTERNATE LIVELIHOOD TRAINING AND SUPPORT TO COMMITTEES, DEVELOP EDUCATION MODULES FOR LOCAL EDUCATORS FOR TIGER AND HABITAT CONSERVATION, SET UP A FOUNDATION FOR RESEARCH AT SMTR, AND EVALUATE THE IMPACT OF THE PROJECT.</narrative>
  </description>
